<title>USA: ITT launches $2.1 billion self-tender.</title>
<headline>ITT launches $2.1 billion self-tender.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>ITT Corp on Thursday launched a $2.1 billion buyback of up to 30 million shares at $70 each as part of its massive restructuring announced Wednesday.</p>
<p>Unless extended, the tender offer expires at midnnight August 13.</p>
<p>ITT on Wednesday said it would buy back 26 percent of its outstanding common shares, split the company into three pieces, and buy back $2.0 billion of debt.</p>
<p>The moves are part of its effort to thwart a $6.5 billion hostile takeover by rival Hilton Hotels Corp.</p>
<p>Shares of ITT were off 5/8 to 66-3/8 in early trade.</p>
<p>(--Robin Sidel, 212/859-1723)</p>
</text>
